-- personal_relationships (17)
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(e'A woman discovers her brother has been quietly paying her rent for two years without telling her. She had believed the studio was rent-controlled. When she finds out, she stops accepting his money, repays what she can, and moves to a smaller flat she can afford on her own. Her brother is hurt — he says she has taken away something he wanted to give.', e'Was she right to refuse the help?', 'Family · Pride', 'Right to refuse', 'Wrong to refuse', 'Adult independence is not a debt to anyone.', 'Help offered in love does not become an insult.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man finds his wife’s old diary while clearing out a cupboard. He reads it cover to cover. It contains nothing she has hidden from him — only feelings she once had, and never spoke aloud. He tells her about it weeks later, in an argument.', e'Was reading it justified?', 'Marriage · Trust', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'Curiosity in a shared home is not a betrayal.', 'Privacy is the floor a marriage stands on.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A daughter cuts off contact with her father after he refuses to apologize for something he said at her wedding. Two years pass. He is diagnosed with a condition that may shorten his life. She does not return his calls. She believes he is using the diagnosis to manipulate her.', e'Was she right to stay away?', 'Estrangement', 'Right to stay away', 'Wrong to stay away', 'A boundary is not a punishment to be lifted on schedule.', 'There are some doors you do not get a second chance to walk through.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A bride asks her best friend, who is recovering from an eating disorder, not to attend the bachelorette weekend because of how the trip might affect her. The friend is grateful at first, then later furious. She says she felt erased.', e'Was the bride right to ask?', 'Friendship · Care', 'Right to ask', 'Wrong to ask', 'Protecting someone is sometimes the kindest exclusion.', 'Care that decides for someone is not care.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man finds out his cousin has been telling people in their extended family that he is in financial trouble — which is a lie. The cousin says she was trying to deflect attention from her own divorce. He confronts her publicly at a family dinner.', e'Was the public confrontation justified?', 'Family · Honesty', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A lie made public deserves to be corrected in public.', 'A family table is not the right courtroom.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman ends a six-year friendship over a single political argument that has nothing to do with their daily lives. She says the friendship had been hollow for years; the argument simply confirmed it.', e'Was ending it justified?', 'Friendship · Drift', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A long friendship can be honestly outgrown.', 'Six years deserved a conversation, not an exit.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A father refuses to walk his daughter down the aisle because she is marrying someone he does not approve of. He does attend the wedding. He sits in the front row and weeps.', e'Was he right to refuse the walk?', 'Family · Ritual', 'Right to refuse', 'Wrong to refuse', 'A blessing cannot be performed if it is not felt.', 'A wedding day is not the day for a private protest.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman’s mother-in-law moves in for what was supposed to be a month of recovery after surgery. Eight months later she is still there, and the woman is exhausted. She asks her husband to set a deadline. He refuses. She tells her mother-in-law herself.', e'Was she justified in telling her directly?', 'In-laws · Boundaries', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'Her home is also her home.', 'It should have gone through her husband.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man tells his pregnant partner he does not want to be present at the birth because he is afraid he will faint and embarrass her. He offers to be in the next room. She is hurt and goes through it alone.', e'Was he right to step back?', 'Parenting · Fear', 'Right to step back', 'Wrong to step back', 'Honest fear is better than a forced presence.', 'A birth is not a place to manage your image.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman secretly takes a DNA test that confirms her uncle is, in fact, her biological father. She tells no one. She lets her mother and her uncle live out their lives in the family they built around the lie.', e'Was she right to stay silent?', 'Family · Secrets', 'Right to stay silent', 'Wrong to stay silent', 'A truth without a use case can be a cruelty.', 'Everyone in that house had a right to know.', 'personal_relationships', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A man discovers that his teenage son has been bullying a classmate online for months. He makes his son write a public apology, hand-deliver it to the classmate’s parents, and quit the football team his son loves.', e'Was the punishment proportionate?', 'Parenting · Discipline', 'Proportionate', 'Excessive', 'Cruelty learned young is hardest to unlearn later.', 'A teenager broken in public learns shame, not change.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman in her forties refuses to attend her sister’s wedding because the sister has invited their estranged father. The bride says the day is not about the sister; the sister says the invitation is.', e'Was she right to skip it?', 'Family · Loyalty', 'Right to skip', 'Wrong to skip', 'You do not have to share a room with someone you’ve survived.', 'A sister’s day is not the right day to draw the line.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man pays for his sister’s wedding entirely out of pocket — about eight months of his salary — and never mentions the cost. She finds out from a cousin a year later, and confronts him for not letting her contribute.', e'Was he right to hide it?', 'Family · Generosity', 'Right to hide it', 'Wrong to hide it', 'A gift declared is a gift weighed.', 'Adults deserve to know what they are accepting.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman tells her best friend that her fiancé made a pass at her at a party. The friend confronts the fiancé, who denies it. The wedding is called off. Months later, the friend admits she may have misread the moment.', e'Was she right to tell her?', 'Friendship · Loyalty', 'Right to tell', 'Wrong to tell', 'Silence about something like that is its own kind of betrayal.', 'A single ambiguous moment is not worth a marriage.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A grandmother refuses to babysit her grandchild during the week, saying she raised her own children and is now retired. Her daughter, a single mother, is forced to leave a job she loves for one with daycare hours.', e'Was the grandmother justified?', 'Family · Generations', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'Retirement is a stage no one else gets to schedule.', 'Family is the obligation you do not get to retire from.', 'personal_relationships', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man asks his partner of nine years to sign a postnuptial agreement before they buy a house together. She agrees but says something between them has now permanently shifted. He thinks she is being unfair.', e'Was he right to ask?', 'Marriage · Money', 'Right to ask', 'Wrong to ask', 'A clear paper protects an unclear future.', 'Nine years should not need a contract.', 'personal_relationships', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A woman writes a long letter to her father, who died fifteen years ago, telling him everything she could not say while he was alive. She reads it at a family gathering on his death anniversary. Some relatives find it healing. Others find it cruel to his memory.', e'Was she right to read it aloud?', 'Family · Grief', 'Right to read', 'Wrong to read', 'Grief does not have to be quiet to be respectful.', 'A man unable to defend himself deserved a private goodbye.', 'personal_relationships', 'seasonal', 'curated'),

