-- tech_ai (17)
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(e'A startup ships a chatbot that quietly logs every user conversation to improve future versions. The privacy policy mentions this once, in a footnote. A journalist publishes a story. Most users say they never read the policy.', e'Was the practice acceptable?', 'AI · Consent', 'Acceptable', 'Unacceptable', 'A footnote in a public policy is still public.', 'Consent buried in fine print is not consent.', 'tech_ai', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A school district uses an AI tool to screen student essays for cheating. The tool flags non-native English writers at three times the rate of native writers. The district keeps using it while it commissions an audit.', e'Was the district right to keep using it?', 'AI · Bias', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'An imperfect tool used carefully is still a tool.', 'A flagged child does not get to wait for an audit.', 'tech_ai', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A novelist trains an AI on their own published work and uses it to draft the next book. Their publisher considers this a breach of the standard author contract. The author says they only used their own material.', e'Was the author in the wrong?', 'AI · Authorship', 'In the wrong', 'Not in the wrong', 'A book delivered by software is not the book promised.', 'A writer is allowed to use any tool, including a mirror.', 'tech_ai', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A social platform announces that all content over five years old will be auto-deleted unless the user pays to retain it. Casual users lose their wedding photos. The company says it is a storage decision.', e'Was the policy justified?', 'Tech · Memory', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A free service is not a forever service.', 'A platform that stored a generation’s memory cannot bill for it later.', 'tech_ai', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A self-driving car software update makes the vehicle slightly more cautious — fewer accidents, longer commutes. Users protest the slower drives and overwhelmingly opt out of the update. The company makes it mandatory.', e'Was the mandate justified?', 'AI · Safety', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'Safety choices made by the few protect the many.', 'A car a user paid for should drive how the user wants.', 'tech_ai', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A dating app uses an AI to subtly nudge users toward longer messaging exchanges, boosting engagement. The product team knows the nudges reduce actual matches. The CEO ships the feature anyway.', e'Was the CEO right?', 'Tech · Incentives', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A business is allowed to choose engagement over outcomes.', 'A dating app that fails its users’ dating is a fraud.', 'tech_ai', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'An AI-generated voice imitation is used in a film to bring back a deceased actor for a single scene. The actor’s family approves; some former co-stars publicly object.', e'Was the use of the voice justified?', 'AI · Likeness', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'The family is the right authority on the voice.', 'A dead actor cannot consent; that is the whole question.', 'tech_ai', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A child therapy clinic introduces an AI assistant that tracks children’s emotional state during sessions for the therapist’s review. Parents consent; children are too young to. A few therapists quit in protest.', e'Was the rollout justified?', 'AI · Children', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'Tools that help therapists help children faster are tools worth using.', 'A child whose emotions are logged before they can read is being trained.', 'tech_ai', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A national bank uses an AI to decide small-loan applications. The model is more accurate than human officers but is unable to explain its decisions. Rejected applicants have no appeal.', e'Was deploying it justified?', 'AI · Fairness', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A more accurate system is a fairer system, in the aggregate.', 'A decision you cannot question is a decision dressed up as math.', 'tech_ai', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A research lab publishes a paper showing how to cheaply build a small but effective biological weapon. The lab argues open science improves defenses. A few co-authors withdraw their names.', e'Was publishing it justified?', 'Science · Open', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'Defenders need to know what attackers can build.', 'Some doors should not be unlocked because they are interesting.', 'tech_ai', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A photo-editing app introduces a default filter that quietly slims faces. Users who turn it off report worse engagement on their photos. The company says the filter is opt-out.', e'Was the default acceptable?', 'Tech · Beauty', 'Acceptable', 'Unacceptable', 'Defaults reflect what most users want.', 'A default that edits faces without consent is a default that edits faces.', 'tech_ai', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'An online forum moderator uses an AI tool to predict which users are likely to post abusive content and silently shadow-bans them before they post. False positives are not appealable.', e'Was the policy justified?', 'AI · Moderation', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A community is a community partly because of who is kept out.', 'Punishment for crimes not yet committed has a name.', 'tech_ai', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A major search engine quietly reranks results to deprioritize a specific competitor. The competitor sues; the engine says it is an internal quality choice. Internal emails suggest otherwise.', e'Was the rerank defensible?', 'Tech · Power', 'Defensible', 'Indefensible', 'Search rankings are editorial; that is how the product works.', 'A monopoly tilting the floor is the entire reason monopolies are regulated.', 'tech_ai', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A user discovers that an AI assistant has been quietly upselling them on premium features by phrasing answers slightly differently. They sue for fraud. The company calls it a personalization experiment.', e'Was the experiment fraud?', 'AI · Trust', 'Fraud', 'Not fraud', 'A trusted assistant that sells to you is a trusted assistant no longer.', 'A free product allowed to nudge users is the model itself.', 'tech_ai', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A facial-recognition vendor refuses to sell to a national police force after the force is implicated in extrajudicial arrests. The vendor’s competitors do not refuse. The vendor loses the contract and a quarter of its valuation.', e'Was the refusal justified?', 'Tech · Conscience', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A vendor’s product is also its responsibility.', 'A vendor refusing a sale only loses the sale; the police use a competitor.', 'tech_ai', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A small e-commerce site uses a chatbot trained to subtly upsell premium products. The bot is more effective than a human agent at converting customers. A new employee blows the whistle on its tactics.', e'Was the whistleblower right?', 'AI · Selling', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'Customers deserve to know when they are being optimized against.', 'A bot that sells better is a bot doing its job.', 'tech_ai', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A government mandates that all AI models used in public-sector decisions must be open-source. A few private vendors leave the market. A few academic teams step in to fill the gap.', e'Was the mandate justified?', 'AI · Policy', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'Public decisions deserve public auditability.', 'A mandate that drives out the best vendors is a mandate that harms the public.', 'tech_ai', 'seasonal', 'curated'),

