-- love_romance (16)
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(e'A man proposes to his partner of seven years on a busy public street, surrounded by strangers and cameras. She says yes. Later, she tells him she had asked him a year ago never to propose in public.', e'Was the public proposal wrong?', 'Love · Boundaries', 'Wrong', 'Not wrong', 'A proposal that ignores a stated wish is a proposal about the proposer.', 'A grand gesture is the whole language of love.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman tells her boyfriend on their second date that she has decided she does not want children. He says he understands. Two years later, he begins to lobby her on the question.', e'Was she right to leave him?', 'Love · Children', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A stated terms is a stated terms; she was clear.', 'Love sometimes changes what we said early.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man tells his ex-wife the night before her remarriage that he still loves her. She marries the next day anyway, but the marriage starts under a shadow.', e'Was he right to tell her?', 'Love · Timing', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A truth held back becomes a regret.', 'A truth deployed the day before a wedding is sabotage in feeling’s clothes.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman moves to a new country for her partner. She struggles to find work for a year. He grows distant, then ends the relationship. She has no roots in the new country and limited savings.', e'Did she make a mistake moving?', 'Love · Risk', 'Mistake', 'Not a mistake', 'A move predicated on a single relationship is a move you cannot afford.', 'A life lived in caution is a life lived alone.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man stays in an unhappy relationship for the sake of a child he and his partner are raising together. The child is six. The unhappiness is well-hidden but constant.', e'Was he right to stay?', 'Love · Children', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A stable home for a six-year-old is a real gift.', 'A child raised on hidden unhappiness learns it as love.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman discovers her partner of two years has been keeping in close contact with an ex. The messages are not romantic, but they are constant. She asks him to stop. He calls her insecure.', e'Was she right to ask?', 'Love · Boundaries', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A boundary asked for is not the same as a boundary imposed.', 'A partner does not get to dictate other friendships.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man tells his partner that he has been in love with someone else for the past year but has done nothing about it. She thanks him for his honesty. She also leaves him within a week.', e'Did he do the right thing?', 'Love · Honesty', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A confession that costs the confessor is the kind that is honest.', 'A confession someone never had to make is a confession that served only him.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman reads her partner’s private journal during an argument. She finds nothing damning but learns he sometimes feels disappointed in their life together. She does not tell him she read it. The relationship continues.', e'Was the reading a betrayal?', 'Love · Privacy', 'Betrayal', 'Not a betrayal', 'A private journal is the last private place a partner has.', 'A relationship under tension justifies a look.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man tells his partner he is going on a solo trip to think about whether to propose. He returns engaged in his head; she has decided in his absence that she wants to end the relationship.', e'Was the solo trip wise?', 'Love · Space', 'Wise', 'Unwise', 'A decision worth making is worth thinking about alone.', 'A decision about two people made by one absent person is a decision made wrongly.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman ends an arranged engagement after meeting her fiancé three times. Both families had finalized the wedding. She returns the ring. She is criticized by both sides for wasting their time.', e'Was she right to end it?', 'Love · Arranged', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A wedding is forever; three meetings is a sample.', 'A family invests heavily in these things; you owe them more than three meetings.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man pays for his partner’s entire MBA, with no agreement about repayment. She graduates and immediately ends the relationship. He asks for a partial refund. She refuses.', e'Was he right to ask?', 'Love · Money', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A gift in a relationship is conditional on the relationship.', 'A gift is a gift; if you wanted a loan, you should have papered it.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A long-distance couple sets a rule that they will tell each other every time they go on a date with someone else. One of them stops mentioning a particular person. The other finds out months later.', e'Was the silence a breach?', 'Love · Honesty', 'Breach', 'Not a breach', 'A rule both agreed to is a rule both keep.', 'A particular silence is not a confession of betrayal.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A woman’s partner asks her to delete all photos of her exes from her phone. She refuses, calling it controlling. He says it is a minor request. They break up over it.', e'Was she right to refuse?', 'Love · Trust', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A relationship that requires erasing your past is a relationship asking too much.', 'A small ask for peace of mind is not a price of admission.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man tells his partner he is bisexual after five years of marriage. She thanks him for telling her. She also says it changes something for her she cannot describe. They divorce two years later.', e'Did he do the right thing?', 'Love · Truth', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A truth he carried alone needed to be shared.', 'A truth that arrives five years late is a truth that should have arrived earlier.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A widow finds love again three years after losing her husband. Her adult children ask her to wait longer “for the family.” She does not. The new relationship is welcomed by half the family and avoided by the other.', e'Was she right to move on?', 'Love · Grief', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A life remaining is a life to be lived.', 'A family is a witness to a life; their pace deserves respect.', 'love_romance', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A man cancels his wedding three days before the ceremony after a private conversation with the bride’s sister in which she revealed something he could not unhear. He never tells the bride what was said.', e'Was he right to stay silent?', 'Love · Secrets', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A wedding cancelled is enough; details destroy two relationships.', 'A bride called off three days before a wedding deserves to know why.', 'love_romance', 'seasonal', 'curated'),

