-- the_future (16)
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
(e'A government offers cash incentives for couples to have a third child after a long decline in birth rates. Activists call it coercive. The first cohort of incentivized births arrives a year later.', e'Was the incentive justified?', 'Future · Demography', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A country without children has no future to plan for.', 'A child born for a subsidy is a child born for the wrong reason.', 'the_future', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A research institute extends average life expectancy by twenty years with a treatment available only to the wealthiest. Demand for it outstrips public funding. The treatment remains private.', e'Was the institute wrong to launch it?', 'Future · Longevity', 'Wrong', 'Not wrong', 'A two-tier life expectancy is a two-tier civilization.', 'A new treatment starts where it can; access widens later.', 'the_future', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A school replaces a quarter of its teaching staff with adaptive software. Test scores hold steady; satisfaction drops. The school says results matter; some parents disagree.', e'Was the substitution justified?', 'Future · Education', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A child taught well by software is a child taught well.', 'A school without teachers has stopped being a school.', 'the_future', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A national government introduces a universal basic income at a modest level, paid for by a sharp wealth tax. Some wealthy citizens emigrate. Many families breathe for the first time in years.', e'Was the policy justified?', 'Future · Economy', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A floor under every family is a country worth its name.', 'A tax that drives out builders impoverishes the country it claims to help.', 'the_future', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A city legalizes fully autonomous taxis with no human oversight. Crashes drop by 30%. Many taxi drivers are pushed out of work without retraining programs in place.', e'Was the city right?', 'Future · Work', 'Right', 'Wrong', 'A 30% drop in crashes is a 30% drop in funerals.', 'A city that replaces workers without retraining is a city that broke a promise.', 'the_future', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A government bans children under 15 from social media. Parents who allow it are fined. Some parents argue it removes a useful channel for their introverted children.', e'Was the ban justified?', 'Future · Childhood', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A childhood lost to feeds is the design’s fault, not the family’s.', 'A parent is the right authority on a child, not the state.', 'the_future', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A national identity database links every citizen’s health, work, and travel records. Efficiency improves. A few cases of misuse leak. Officials promise tighter controls.', e'Was the database justified?', 'Future · State', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A modern state runs on coordinated data.', 'A database that knows everything about everyone is a database one decision away from misuse.', 'the_future', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A workplace introduces continuous productivity monitoring, including biometrics. High performers cite no problem. Lower performers leave. The company calls it a fair filter.', e'Was the system justified?', 'Future · Surveillance', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A workplace allowed to measure outcomes is a workplace doing its job.', 'A workplace that monitors heartbeats has lost what a workplace is for.', 'the_future', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A research lab proves that early genetic screening of fetuses can prevent several common conditions. Insurance begins requiring the screening. Families who refuse face higher premiums.', e'Was the requirement justified?', 'Future · Genetics', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A health system that prevents conditions cheaply should require what it can.', 'A health system that prices choice out of families is a coercive one.', 'the_future', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A small country grants legal personhood to a major river. Polluters can now be sued by the river itself, through court-appointed guardians. A foreign mining company calls the law absurd.', e'Was the law justified?', 'Future · Nature', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A river that can sue is a river that can survive.', 'Legal fictions invented to win lawsuits are a slope, not a stand.', 'the_future', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A government mandates that all generated media be tagged with a non-removable watermark identifying its origin. Independent artists worry about provenance ambiguity. Disinformation drops measurably.', e'Was the mandate justified?', 'Future · Truth', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A public sphere without provenance is a public sphere without truth.', 'A watermark mandated by the state is a watermark that follows you home.', 'the_future', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A city permits a single private company to operate all public transit, in exchange for a guaranteed price cap and 24-hour service. Two years later the cap holds; coverage is better; civic groups call the deal undemocratic.', e'Was the deal worth it?', 'Future · Civic', 'Worth it', 'Not worth it', 'A working bus is the test of governance; not who runs it.', 'A city contracted out is a city without a public spine.', 'the_future', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A regulator allows companies to sell genetic test results to advertisers if customers consent. A clear opt-out is provided. The opt-out is checked by a small minority. The market explodes.', e'Was the regulator wrong?', 'Future · Consent', 'Wrong', 'Not wrong', 'Consent buried under a default is consent shaped by design.', 'A market built on clear opt-outs is a market that respects choice.', 'the_future', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A national government bans cryptocurrencies entirely. Citizens lose access to overseas savings. Black markets emerge. The ban achieves its stated objectives in part.', e'Was the ban justified?', 'Future · Money', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A currency outside the state is a currency the state cannot tax fairly.', 'A ban that creates a black market is a ban that empowered the criminals it claimed to fight.', 'the_future', 'topical', 'curated'),
(e'A space agency proposes a permanent off-world settlement funded jointly by several countries. Critics call it a vanity project while many earthly problems remain unsolved. The agency proceeds.', e'Was the project justified?', 'Future · Frontier', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'A species with somewhere else to live is a species that survives the next millennium.', 'A planet whose problems are unsolved should not pay for another planet first.', 'the_future', 'evergreen', 'curated'),
(e'A government legalizes brain-computer interfaces for medical use, with off-label use loosely policed. Within five years, executives in several industries adopt them. The labor advantage compounds.', e'Was the loose policing justified?', 'Future · Body', 'Justified', 'Not justified', 'Innovation requires room to be misused before it is shaped.', 'A device that compounds advantage is a device that decides the next generation.', 'the_future', 'seasonal', 'curated');

commit;
